{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793205713,"nonce":"FVNuX0E8U9RnYWYvFWkRnbubQHY=","title":"Stateless app tree rendering loses visual group isolation","message":"RenderContext::render_tree uses a separate layered walker and collection/dispatch path. Shapes in an ordinary opacity group are rendered fully opaque while collected text/images are drawn later, outside the group effects. A native canvas rectangle inside a 50%-opacity group on blue rendered [0,255,0,255] instead of [0,128,127,255]. Reproduced before production changes on b8c251af6ada7126efba99d2a269c481be7b52c9; log /private/tmp/blinc-snapshot-negative.log.\n\nSeven existing legacy controls passed before changing production: four main text clip, one legacy mixed boundary, one foreground RGBA application sequence and one application image clip sequence. Baseline logs /private/tmp/blinc-snapshot-baseline-*.log.\n\nScoped fix: reuse the current collected-content/ordered frame pipeline for the stateless public app entry, with optional entry/exit animation state in the layout walker. A stateless frame must not construct a RenderState or change the global animation scheduler. Keep snapshot/animated cache ownership distinct and release snapshot replay batches/promoted textures after dispatch. Preserve direct/animated/compositor and existing clipping/feature behavior while correcting supported stateless group composition.\n\nThis is a child of e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a. General unsupported glass/global-overlay/3D ancestors, independent GPU passes/meshes, arbitrary cross-pass named textures, low-level separate-context layout painting and other remaining owners are not closed by unifying the app frame entry. No source/tracker push or publishing.","files":null}]}